        content: "<ol>\n<li><strong>Find the legal entity.</strong> The app's brand can differ from the licensed company named in its terms or website footer.</li>\n<li><strong>Look it up on the official register</strong> for the country you send from (table below): name, status and any restrictions.</li>\n<li><strong>Check the license type.</strong> Bank, e-money institution, payment institution and money transmitter carry different protection. In the UK, a small payment institution has no duty to safeguard.</li>\n<li><strong>Read the safeguarding section of the terms.</strong> It should say whether money sits in a separate account or is covered by insurance, and that the firm is not a bank.</li>\n<li><strong>Watch for red flags:</strong> a non-bank claiming FSCS or FDIC protection for its own balances, interest offered on money waiting to be sent, or an offer to hold your money with no payment instruction. Premier FX did all three.</li>\n</ol>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Country</th><th>Where to check</th><th>What a listing tells you</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>UK</td><td><a href=\"https://register.fca.org.uk/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FCA Register</a></td><td>Firm type and status; the FSCS does not cover e-money or payment firms failing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>EU / EEA</td><td>Home country regulator's register; <a href=\"https://www.eba.europa.eu/risk-and-data-analysis/data/registers/payment-institutions-register\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">EBA register</a></td><td>License and passport; the EBA copy has no legal force</td></tr>\n<tr><td>US</td><td><a href=\"https://www.nmlsconsumeraccess.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NMLS Consumer Access</a></td><td>Whether the firm is authorized in your state</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Canada</td><td><a href=\"https://www.bankofcanada.ca/regulatory-oversight/retail-payments/psp-registry/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bank of Canada PSP registry</a>; <a href=\"https://fintrac-canafe.canada.ca/msb-esm/reg-eng\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FINTRAC MSB registry</a></td><td>Registered, not licensed or endorsed</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Australia</td><td><a href=\"https://www.austrac.gov.au/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AUSTRAC</a>, the anti-money-laundering regulator</td><td>Registered for anti-money-laundering purposes; no deposit guarantee</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Money transfer app balances vs sending straight through</h3>\n<p>Your money is exposed only while the company holds it. A transfer paid out the same day is at risk for hours or days; a balance in an e-money account is at risk for as long as it sits there, and the FSCS warns it \"could be tied up for a while during the insolvency process.\" Fund a transfer when you are ready to send, and keep savings in a bank within the deposit insurance limit. At Premier FX, money customers left with the firm to hold was mixed with other customers' money and the firm's own the moment it arrived, the FCA found.</p>",
