        answer: "Only for some payments. UK and EU rules require the money to reach the recipient's bank by the end of the next business day for sterling payments within the UK and for euro payments within the UK and EEA, such as SEPA transfers. The FCA's guidance and PSD2 Article 2(4) switch the limit off for transfers to banks outside the UK and EEA. For those transfers, the provider's terms set the time.",
